# Patterns here are matched against the path relative to the build context
# root, so an entry without a slash only matches at the root level.
#
# `xroute` below therefore excludes the compiled binary at the repo root
# and NOT cmd/xroute/ — which is the package the Dockerfile builds. Widening
# it to `**/xroute` would empty cmd/xroute/ out of the context and the
# build would fail with no Go files. Same for `xroute-*`.
#
# `*.pgo` must never be added: cmd/xroute/default.pgo is what Go's default
# -pgo=auto consumes, and dropping it from the context silently produces an
# unoptimized binary that still builds fine. The `docker` job in ci.yml asserts
# it is still in the image.
.git
.github
node_modules
web/node_modules
web/dist
xroute
xroute-*
*.exe
*.test
*.out
*.log
.xroute
data
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
graphify-out
stitch-screens
stitch-screenshots
